note as OresMarketdataCoreFreeFunctions
    Free functions in ores::marketdata::core:
    classification_key_of(d : const datum::market_datum&) : classification_key
    make_pillar_quote_key(ccy, start_tenor_code : const string&, start_date, end_date : chrono::year_month_day) : pillar_quote_key
    pillar_series_uri(key : const pillar_quote_key&) : string
    pillar_datum_uri(key : const pillar_quote_key&) : string
    classification_key_of reads the series type, metric and qualifier that
    the classification rules are keyed by out of an ORE key. make_pillar_quote_key
    builds one curve pillar's quote key from the currency and the pillar's own
    dates, and the two URI functions project it: pillar_series_uri drops the
    point for the series identity, pillar_datum_uri keeps it for the datum.
end note

note as OresMarketdataRepositoryHelpers
    Free functions in ores::marketdata::repository:
    as_of_observation(row : const as_of_row&, first : size_t, read : string_view) : market_observation_entity
    as_of_bucket_ordinal(row : const as_of_row&, bucket_count : size_t) : size_t
    operator<<(s : ostream&, v : const T&) : ostream&
    as_of_observation reads the ten observation columns of an as-of read row
    from column first on and throws std::runtime_error when the row is short.
    as_of_bucket_ordinal reads the bucket ordinal the row's first column carries
    and throws unless it is all digits and below bucket_count. The operator is
    emitted for all seven entities: feed_binding, market_fixing,
    market_observation, market_series, market_series_asset_class,
    observation_lineage and series_classification_rule. as_of_row itself is a
    namespace-scope alias, using as_of_row = vector<optional<string>>, and has no
    box either.
end note

